“Essential Docker Commands Every DevOps Engineer Should Know”

🔹 Basic Docker Commands

docker --version → Check Docker version
docker info → Show system-wide Docker info
docker help → List all commands

🔹 Container Commands

docker ps → List running containers
docker ps -a → List all containers (including stopped)
docker run -it ubuntu /bin/bash → Run container interactively
docker start <container_id> → Start a stopped container
docker stop <container_id> → Stop a running container
docker restart <container_id> → Restart container
docker rm <container_id> → Remove container

🔹 Image Commands

docker images → List images
docker pull nginx → Download an image
docker build -t myapp:1.0 . → Build image from Dockerfile
docker rmi <image_id> → Remove image

🔹 Logs, Exec & Inspect

docker logs <container_id> → View container logs
docker exec -it <container_id> bash → Access running container shell
docker inspect <container_id> → Detailed container info

🔹 Docker Volumes & Networks

docker volume ls → List volumes
docker network ls → List networks
docker network inspect bridge → Inspect network

🔹 System Cleanup

docker system prune → Remove unused containers, networks, images
docker image prune → Remove dangling images
docker container prune → Remove stopped containers

⚡ Pro Tip:
 Use docker-compose for multi-container apps:

docker-compose up -d   # Start services  
docker-compose down    # Stop & remove services  
